# AI2 review — demo-v022, v5 round 6

**FAIL for shipping at the current 1920 × 1080 working resolution.** The problem, mechanism, saved evaluation and closing SEC proof are understandable and well supported. The new wait-window narration does not satisfy the Owner's sync gate. Two transcript additions also fail the requested source-fidelity test. **42 of 48 ledger rows can be confirmed as written; six are blockers or unconfirmable as specified.** The submitted automated “0 fails” does not establish semantic synchronization.

Reviewed 2026-11-04, read-only. Scope: the actual local v022 MP4/SRT, all 398 raw plus 398 captioned review PNGs, keyframes, current 48-row ledger, saved OCR evidence, the 20261104T170659731519Z receipts and pod log, and the real local CLI session. The prompt's “240 frames / 43 rows / ocr-20” describes an earlier bundle: the present bundle has 398 indexed times, 48 rows and `ocr-25.json`. Current checkout is `demo/v5` at `ed71ce698f779f4fcf17fa8228de08578c04fc6e`, rather than the cited `aa3e313e`; this verdict is tied to the file hashes below, not an assumption about that commit's contents. No recorder, synthesis, video render, model call, SEC fetch or network request was run. Only this report was written inside the repository.

## Numbered shipping blockers

1. **B1 — Wait-window picture does not show the narrated event/count. Film 1:06.056–1:20.141.** At **66.056–68.291**, “Muse Spark calls the SEC tools” accompanies the command and `model reasoning … step 1`, with no actual tool call. The first call appears at **68.567**, **2.511 s after speech starts and 0.276 s after it finishes**. See [frame-1981-066.033s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v022/frame-1981-066.033s.png) (provided reference: [keyframe-135-66p056s.png](/Users/yan/git/market-claim-verifier-video/demo/out/review-v5/captioned/keyframe-135-66p056s.png)) and the first call [frame-2057-068.567s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v022/frame-2057-068.567s.png). At **68.506–69.346**, “Four claims” only changes the terminal title color: no four-claim list or count appears ([frame-2055-068.500s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v022/frame-2055-068.500s.png) (provided reference: [keyframe-144-68p506s.png](/Users/yan/git/market-claim-verifier-video/demo/out/review-v5/captioned/keyframe-144-68p506s.png))). At **69.546–71.256**, “Four SEC lookups” has no explicit four-call state; the rolling window mixes calls and results, including `compute_change` ([frame-2086-069.533s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v022/frame-2086-069.533s.png) (provided reference: [keyframe-155-69p546s.png](/Users/yan/git/market-claim-verifier-video/demo/out/review-v5/captioned/keyframe-155-69p546s.png))). The source contains **three `lookup_fact` calls and one `compute_change` call**, and the result contains four checked factual claims plus two unchecked opinions. At **78.856–80.141**, “Then the program decides” still shows `model reasoning … step 2`; the first actual `program_check`/verdict rows arrive at **81.833**, **2.978 s after speech starts** ([frame-2365-078.833s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v022/frame-2365-078.833s.png) (provided reference: [keyframe-186-78p856s.png](/Users/yan/git/market-claim-verifier-video/demo/out/review-v5/captioned/keyframe-186-78p856s.png)); first decision [frame-2455-081.833s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v022/frame-2455-081.833s.png)).

   **Exact fix:** retain the real event timestamps. Put the tools sentence at **68.700** with the first call visibly focused from **68.567**; put the decision sentence at **81.970** and retain the program-check state through its end, about **83.255**. Move the following verdict sentence to about **83.450**, with its citation card ready by **83.300**; the existing draft sentence at 85.574 still fits. Re-sequence the short intervening phrases into the remaining wait interval. Add separate, clearly editorial annotations **“4 factual claims”** and **“4 tool calls: 3 lookups + 1 calculation”**, each arriving 0–0.5 s before its own phrase and remaining for the whole phrase. Use “four tool calls” in narration. A green title, command, or underlined clock cannot stand in for those named states. Recheck every affected sentence after the recut.

2. **B2 — Clock is described as the wrong measurement. Film 1:14.856–1:16.806.** “The clock is the model's thinking time” is false for this stopwatch. It starts with the request at film **65.8556**, includes preprocessing and the SEC-tool interval, and stops at the request's roughly 16-second verdict. At film **74.867** it shows **9.0 s**, while step 2 began at about **69.876**; that phase has run for about 5.0 s. This is not an isolated model-time counter or a cumulative model-only counter. See [frame-2246-074.867s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v022/frame-2246-074.867s.png) (provided reference: [keyframe-175-74p856s.png](/Users/yan/git/market-claim-verifier-video/demo/out/review-v5/captioned/keyframe-175-74p856s.png)); implementation [live-terminal.mjs](/Users/yan/git/market-claim-verifier-video/demo/motion/v5/live-terminal.mjs) (`elapsed = local − start_scene_s`). **Exact fix:** label the stopwatch **“Request elapsed”** and change that sentence/SRT to **“The clock shows elapsed time for this request.”** Keep the genuine total; do not relabel it as model time. Re-measure the replacement sentence and its visual lead.

3. **B3 — Two displayed transcript lines are additions rather than source rows. Film about 1:05.9–1:08.5 and 2:00.100–2:00.800.** The online terminal prints **`$ claimcheck post post.txt --provider baseten --budget 1`**. That command does not occur anywhere in this request's pod log; this was a web request. See [frame-1981-066.033s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v022/frame-1981-066.033s.png). The real local PTY ends with JSON, but the displayed final line **`verdict  2 supported · 1 contradicted  $0.0611`** is appended by the presentation compiler; it is absent as a row from `local-cli.json`. Its values are supported by that session, so this is a provenance-label failure, not an invented cost or outcome. See [frame-3603-120.100s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v022/frame-3603-120.100s.png) (provided reference: [keyframe-326-120p095s.png](/Users/yan/git/market-claim-verifier-video/demo/out/review-v5/captioned/keyframe-326-120p095s.png)). **Exact fix:** remove the online pseudo-command from the server-log replay. In the local replay, pin the actual source receipt row, **`cli +38.32s event=receipt claims=4 supported=2 contradicted=1 insufficient_evidence=0 cost=$0.0611`**, when its source chunk arrives, preserving that source timestamp. Alternatively move a derived receipt summary outside the transcript and label it explicitly **“Receipt summary”**. Every row inside a terminal presented as recorded output must then map to a source event/chunk. Keep the source files unchanged.

4. **B4 — Honesty labels are below the requested 28 px mono minimum. Film 1:05.9–1:22.6 and 1:56.0–2:00.8.** Terminal titles, body rows and clocks are 28 px, but the source/replay footers **“live request 145a6982 · pod log”** and **“replayed at 11×”** are **22 px**. These are the labels a judge needs to distinguish a real request from an accelerated recording. See [frame-1981-066.033s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v022/frame-1981-066.033s.png) and [frame-3499-116.633s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v022/frame-3499-116.633s.png); [style.css](/Users/yan/git/market-claim-verifier-video/demo/motion/v5/style.css) sets `.terminal-window footer` to `font-size:22px`. **Exact fix:** raise these to at least **28 px mono**, allocate their own header space or second line, and reflow the title/clock so all three remain clear without overlap. Verify the final encoded pixels at both resolutions used for review.

5. **B5 — Local-run ledger still promises a final receipt during a sentence that ends before it appears. Film 1:56.175–1:58.460; receipt first at 2:00.100.** Row `v506-01` requires “command, timestamped progress and final receipt.” At the independent speech onset, the command is still typing; at speech end, the session is still running. The final state is not visible until **120.100**, after speech ends at **118.460**. The large **“Local · CLI · recorded 2026-11-04”** identity is correctly present before and during the sentence, so the spoken general statement passes; the written ledger requirement cannot be signed off. See [frame-3486-116.200s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v022/frame-3486-116.200s.png) / [frame-3603-120.100s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v022/frame-3603-120.100s.png) and [sync-ledger.json](/Users/yan/git/market-claim-verifier-video/demo/out/review-v5/sync-ledger.json). **Exact fix:** make this row require **“Local · CLI · recorded identity; real command-line area with typing or recorded output; 11× replay disclosure”**, held for the full sentence. Annotate the later progress arrivals at their actual replay times. Record the final receipt separately as a verified silent hold **120.100–120.800**, after B3 is fixed. Do not claim that receipt was on screen at 116.2 or move the real receipt ahead of its source time.

## Polish items

- **0:08–0:12:** enlarge “Illustrative post” and consider the more specific “Illustrative viral-post scenario.” The small current label can be missed while “Thousands repost it” is narrated; that virality is a story premise, not measured engagement. [keyframe-21-10p400s.png](/Users/yan/git/market-claim-verifier-video/demo/out/review-v5/captioned/keyframe-21-10p400s.png).
- **About 1:36–1:39:** the Apple subtraction card persists while the page moves toward trace/receipt material. It is legal as a hold of the preceding named state, but feels stale during the scroll. Clear it at the trace handoff or retain the Apple native evidence until that handoff. [keyframe-233-99p000s.png](/Users/yan/git/market-claim-verifier-video/demo/out/review-v5/captioned/keyframe-233-99p000s.png).
- **About 1:03–1:05:** the password helper paragraph is now complete above the opaque mask, with no gutter leak. Its last glyphs sit immediately above the mask edge. Give it another 8–12 px of breathing room, or cover the whole helper block between cues; do not reintroduce a paragraph slit.
- **1:56–2:00.8:** 38.57 s of local output is replayed at 11× in a 4.8-second scene including typing. This is honestly disclosed, but a judge can follow only the broad progression. Hold the verbatim receipt longer and spend less of this scene on the JSON tail. Preserve the printed source times and speed disclosure.
- **2:39.250–2:50:** the SEC-result and URL hold is valid and clean, but 10.75 seconds remain after the last URL word. If tightening later, take time from this hold before accelerating a proof scene. The current silent hold is not a sync failure.

## Judge lens and director checks

| Question | Finding |
| --- | --- |
| Problem clear by 0:20? | **Yes.** The Apple amount is a real annual number attached to the wrong quarter; the period error and financial stakes are clear by 19.460. The post is marked illustrative. |
| Mechanism clear by 0:58? | **Yes.** Muse Spark extracts claims and chooses SEC tools; Python performs arithmetic and determines the verdict. “Model proposes; program decides” completes at 57.250. |
| Live proof convincing? | **The final proof is; the wait-window chronology needs B1–B3.** Native verdict plus filing citations, corrected draft, annual-minus-nine-month arithmetic, actual first trace call, program verdict and “Live take” cost/time receipt are all explicitly named and visible. |
| Corrected draft / SEC derivation? | **Confirmed from result JSON.** 416,161,000,000 − 313,695,000,000 = 102,466,000,000: $416.2B − $313.7B = $102.5B at displayed precision. SRT and matched cue text now say “$416.2 billion.” The removed native JSON derivation inspector was never narrated; its removal is a recorded director decision, not a blocker. |
| Headline results honest? | **Yes.** Held-out 240/266 = 90.22556% → 90.2%; one false support among 139 gold non-supported claims; mean cost $0.01987955 → $0.02/claim; median latency 10.01279 s → 10 s/claim. Failures count as wrong. The 1/139 denominator is printed explicitly. |
| Earlier 20.7% / 90.5% comparison? | **Honest with its visible qualifier.** 74/357 versus 323/357, corrected gold, includes dev; this is not the 266-claim held-out denominator. “Saved evaluation” distinguishes it from the live take. The corrected-gold/post-hoc limits in the repository remain part of this claim. |
| Live receipt versus benchmark? | **Separated.** This take is $0.01996865 → $0.0200, about 15.966 s → 16.0 s, four tool calls. “Live take” avoids treating 16.0 s as the held-out 10 s median. Local CLI is a different recorded run, $0.0611; it is not evidence that this web request cost $0.0611. |
| Batch / media honesty? | **Labels are useful; see B4.** The real local recording is labelled recorded/11×. OCR and ASR are labelled saved replays of frozen synthetic inputs, not fresh live media tests. 78 saved Threads attempts have median wall time 6.76481 s → 6.8 s; 72 completed and six failed. 1,000 × 6.8 s = 1.889 h, visibly labelled a sequential one-worker projection, not a measured 1,000-post batch. |
| Ending memorable? | **Yes.** Native corrected amount, both component filing links, a clear filing sentence, URL cue, large URL outro and DappGo wordmark. Both filing links are native anchors, not only an overlay claim. “Fix” is deliberate and accepted. |
| Judge trust risks? | Calling request elapsed time “thinking time”; speaking about a decision before it happens; a pseudo-command in a server log; treating four checked facts as every extracted claim; counting call/result rows as distinct lookups. B1–B3 address these. Native web footage occupies 74/178 s; other product evidence is presented as sourced terminal/evaluation replays. This review does not describe the whole film as unedited live screen capture. |

**Director:** no additional current text collision, caption-over-referent, broken number, unexplained CJK, page-gutter leak, black/dead frame, one-frame native-page hole, or outro collision was found. Web motion overlays are present; the native workspace is centered at 1,560 px width. The cover remains until the Try workspace is framed. The trace cue now lands on the first actual tool-call row. Opaque lower cards/masks protect the named element; the former password and gutter failures are resolved. The native page remains during the closing result hold; both component SEC anchors are exposed. The chapter rail has ten duration-sized segments, correct current labels at the sampled cuts, and no backward progress over the encoded film. At 1, 21, 59, 139 and 171 s its measured fill is about 12, 228, 636, 1500 and 1842 px versus ideal 10.8, 226.5, 636.4, 1499.3 and 1844.5 px; differences are pixel quantization/border width, not a timing error. “Fix” is accepted as directed.

Duration is **178.000 s**, 5,340 frames at 30 fps. Independent FFmpeg loudness analysis gives **−14.18 LUFS, −1.23 dBTP**, inside the Owner limits. The prompt's −14.1/−1.4 is not the exact measurement of this hashed v022 file; v018 measures −14.13/−1.40. This small receipt difference is not a shipping blocker. The final fade is continuous; no black frame occurs before the file ends. Caption lanes stay beneath the rail and do not cover the named native proof. All 48 caption states match the SRT sequence, continuously, with encoded transitions within one 30 fps frame of the cue bounds. Optical presence does not rescue the semantic failures above.

## Independent sync method and confirmation table

The Owner's §11 test is applied to the **named referent for the full phrase**, rather than merely the presence of a card's bounding box. All sentence/phrase rows were independently aligned; the multi-sentence scenes **v501 (5 boundaries), v507 (4), v508 (2), v509 (2)** were not treated as single units. Both disclosure sentences were checked separately too.

1. Decode each MP4's actual audio with FFmpeg to 24 kHz mono PCM; decode all 5,340 picture frames for continuous region, cut, black-frame and rail checks. Extract selected actual encoded frames at full 1920 × 1080 resolution around speech, visual and source-event boundaries. This is decoding for review, not a video render.
2. Resolve each reference cue by its recorded SHA-256 across retained WAV variants; align its waveform to the film audio using FFT normalized cross-correlation of smoothed first differences. Use 5 ms RMS speech bounds at −50 dBFS, checking −48/−52 sensitivity. Minimum correlation: **0.8847 for all 48 v022 cues**, **0.8757 for all 43 v018 cues**. No row depended on the current WAV alias being the historic one.
3. Independently locate visible cue transitions in encoded pixels, inspect the named native region at start/end and through motion, and compare actual log arrival frames to speech. Selected full-resolution proof set: **512 v022 frames and 424 v018 frames**; broad 1-second storyboards and supplied onset/end review frames were inspected as supporting views. The complete supplied bundle was hash-checked. Continuous pixel checks cover the intervening encoded frames; this is not a claim to have manually read every pixel of every frame.
4. Compare film caption-lane image states with the supplied captioned PNG templates and SRT; verify ordering and continuity frame by frame. Recount the results from frozen data, validate the two trace sources independently, and hash-check input preservation. The supplied 25-frame OCR record hashes match its PNGs and reports English-only; manual inspection also found no CJK. An attempted fresh local Vision OCR pass failed with `nilError`; it was retained as a failed attempt and was not counted as an independent OCR pass. No product OCR/ASR was retested.

The ledger is close acoustically, but misses quiet onset by **10 ms at v502-06, 30 ms at v505-14, and 25 ms at v506-01**. These do not change the passing rows. Picture measurements are quantized to 33.333 ms, speech bounds to 5 ms; clear timing margins are larger than those tolerances. **Lead = speech onset minus first frame of the relevant new visual focus.** Positive 0–0.5 s passes only when the correct referent remains present throughout. Negative values mean narration is ahead. A subtitle alone is not proof of a count/event.

