## Source reconciliation for the two real traces

| Source | Independent reconciliation | Limit / required correction |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [serverlog-20261104T170659731519Z.jsonl](/Users/yan/git/market-claim-verifier-video/demo/cache/live-takes/v5/serverlog-20261104T170659731519Z.jsonl) | 21 events: every request ID, event, source argument and relative arrival time agrees with the compiled replay data. Printed time rounding is at most 0.05 s. Request ID `145a6982d1f1459db511db83cb6459dd`; receipt source hash matches. 1× arrival mapping: film 65.855604583 + source elapsed; encoded frame is the ceiling at 30 fps. | B3's online command is an extra illustrative line. Condensed event text is a presentation of source fields, not raw pod-log typography. Same-time event bursts share a frame; the rolling five-row viewport does not make every event readable. |
| [local-cli.json](/Users/yan/git/market-claim-verifier-video/demo/assets/cli-v5/local-cli.json) | 42 PTY chunks, real execution (`dry_run=false`, exit 0, not interrupted), 38.571843 s duration. Actual argv matches the reflowed local command. Accumulated CRLF-normalized text reflowed at 98 characters matches every chunk's displayed tail, apart from the appended summary. Time mapping: film 116.600 + source time / 11. Final source chunk at 38.441306 s maps to 120.094664 s, first encoded frame **3603 / 120.100 s**. | B3's final `verdict …` line is derived, not verbatim PTY output. A source receipt really exists at `cli +38.32s`, delivered in the final chunk. The source-replay speed is 11×, not a 4-second CLI execution. |

All **735 recorded terminal/source hash checks** in the retained asset manifests match. This was independently recomputed; it is supporting provenance, not an excuse for B1's chronology or B3's added rows. The actual online timeline is start +0.01; preprocessing and model step 1 +0.05; first model completion/call +2.69; calls/results +2.98, +3.27, +3.52 and +4.02; second model completion +15.96; program checks and final verdict +15.97. No source timestamp should be moved to fit narration.

The source result's Apple evidence binds the annual and nine-month components to these two saved native links (no live fetching was needed):

- Annual 10-K: `https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320193/000032019326000026/`
- Nine-month 10-Q: `https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320193/000032019326000020/`

## Full-method rerun on v018

**v018 also FAILS**, independently rerun from its MP4 and the archived `review-v5-before-r4-20261104T135135Z` bundle. It is a comparison baseline, not a substitute for v022, and it uses an older take. Its $0.0198 / 14.9 s receipt is not this round's $0.0200 / 16.0 s receipt. The new 20261104T170659731519Z pod log and November 4 local CLI recording are not retroactively attributed to v018.

- **A1 — 1:20.582–1:22.152:** “Contradicted, with the filing” shows the verdict without a filing citation. [frame-2417-080.567s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v018/frame-2417-080.567s.png) (provided reference: [keyframe-127-80p582s.png](/Users/yan/git/market-claim-verifier-video/demo/out/review-v5-before-r4-20261104T135135Z/captioned/keyframe-127-80p582s.png)). Exact fix: retain the contradicted verdict and expose a native filing link or a correctly identified filing citation for the full phrase. **Fixed in v022.**
- **A2 — 0:58 onward and later live-card states:** partial “Reset example”/character-count text and native paragraph fragments remain exposed immediately above/below lower cards; the password helper is not composed cleanly. [frame-1746-058.200s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v018/frame-1746-058.200s.png) (provided reference: [keyframe-111-58p200s.png](/Users/yan/git/market-claim-verifier-video/demo/out/review-v5-before-r4-20261104T135135Z/captioned/keyframe-111-58p200s.png)), [frame-1825-060.833s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v018/frame-1825-060.833s.png), [frame-2417-080.567s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v018/frame-2417-080.567s.png). Exact fix: make the lower mask full-width and opaque through the chapter rail; frame the helper wholly above it or cover it wholly. Preserve the named proof region. **Fixed in v022**, with minor spacing polish still possible.
- **A3 — 2:34.000–2:34.033:** encoded frame **4620** has an empty native-page area at the result cut. [frame-4620-154.000s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v018/frame-4620-154.000s.png); native page returns at [frame-4621-154.033s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v018/frame-4621-154.033s.png). The supplied 154.000 review PNG already contains the page and therefore misses this encoded-frame hole. Exact fix: hold/cover the outgoing frame until the native video frame is ready, or start the native source one frame earlier. **Fixed in v022**, whose actual frame 4620 contains the native filing proof.
- **A4 — 0:35.500–0:38.995:** the old `v503-02` ledger requires 323/357 (90.5%) during the “Give the same model…” phrase, but that number first appears at 39.000. [frame-1065-035.500s.png](/private/tmp/ai2-v022-review-20261104/v018/frame-1065-035.500s.png) (provided reference: [keyframe-79-35p500s.png](/Users/yan/git/market-claim-verifier-video/demo/out/review-v5-before-r4-20261104T135135Z/captioned/keyframe-79-35p500s.png)). The spoken heading itself is correctly timed. Exact fix: make this row describe the SEC-tools/Python heading and qualifier; put 323/357/90.5% on the next “nine in ten” row. **Fixed in v022.**

v018 repeats the clear opening, mechanism and accurate frozen headline numbers, and its ending still exposes both component filing links. All 43 reference cue waveforms match its encoded audio; 43 caption states are continuous and within one frame of the SRT bounds. There are no whole-frame black frames or backward chapter progress. Full-frame review and continuous ROI checks reproduce A1–A4 rather than copying an earlier verdict. **41/43 written ledger requirements can be confirmed; 42/43 spoken referents pass** (A4 is a ledger-description error). v018 does not contain the new real trace replays, so it provides no validation for their source fidelity. It also does not inherit v022's new wait-window sentences.

